WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.360 --> 00:00:05.820
The Golden Globes is a party, and nearly every&nbsp;
celebrity in Hollywood is invited. But it seems&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:05.820 --> 00:00:09.780
a certain contagious disease made its way&nbsp;
onto the guest list as well. Keep watching&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:09.780 --> 00:00:14.280
to find out who won’t be attending any events&nbsp;
for a while, and instead will be back at home.

00:00:14.280 --> 00:00:18.900
It seems that this year's award season is&nbsp;
not going quite as planned. On January 10th,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:18.900 --> 00:00:23.580
2023, the 80th Golden Globe Awards took&nbsp;
place to celebrate the best of film and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:23.580 --> 00:00:27.420
television from the previous year. After&nbsp;
last year's less-than-stellar show that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:27.420 --> 00:00:32.220
saw the Golden Globes go for a hybrid style&nbsp;
of part Zoom and part in-person presentation,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:32.220 --> 00:00:37.440
this year's event brought things back to a more&nbsp;
traditional and welcome manner. The prestigious&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:37.440 --> 00:00:42.300
ceremony saw some pretty major events take place,&nbsp;
from Ke Huy Quan's wholesome best supporting actor&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:42.300 --> 00:00:46.320
win for "Everything Everywhere All At Once"&nbsp;
to Eddie Murphy's Cecil B. DeMille Award win&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:46.320 --> 00:00:49.920
and subsequent speech that referenced&nbsp;
another notable award ceremony moment.

00:00:49.920 --> 00:00:54.180
But as with every year, the Globes couldn't&nbsp;
escape from having some less-than-pleasing&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:54.180 --> 00:00:58.200
moments bog down the festivities. This&nbsp;
year's show brought the ceremony to its&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:58.200 --> 00:01:01.860
lowest ratings yet and continues to see&nbsp;
controversy from within the industry,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:01.860 --> 00:01:06.960
most notably with "The Whale" star Brendan Fraser&nbsp;
skipping out on the event as an act of protest,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:06.960 --> 00:01:10.800
Entertainment Weekly reported. To top it&nbsp;
all off, it seems that several of those&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:10.800 --> 00:01:14.820
who were in attendance took home something&nbsp;
far less desirable than a golden statue.

00:01:14.820 --> 00:01:20.040
Following this year's Golden Globes ceremony,&nbsp;
an uptick in COVID-19 cases has been spreading&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:20.040 --> 00:01:24.420
among some of the night's attendees. First to&nbsp;
report being infected was Jamie Lee Curtis,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:24.420 --> 00:01:28.020
who received a nomination for best supporting&nbsp;
actress for her role in "Everything Everywhere&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:28.020 --> 00:01:31.980
All At Once." The "Halloween" star took to&nbsp;
Instagram on January 13th, where she wrote,

00:01:31.980 --> 00:01:36.480
"F— COVID! Sadly, this head cheerleader&nbsp;
is not going to be at all the weekend&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:36.480 --> 00:01:40.380
festivities cheering on her friends and&nbsp;
colleagues. [Life’s] on life's terms."

00:01:40.380 --> 00:01:43.380
Curtis also shared that, as a&nbsp;
result of the positive test,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:43.380 --> 00:01:47.820
she will not be able to attend either the&nbsp;
BAFTA tea party or Critic Choice Awards,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:47.820 --> 00:01:49.980
despite being nominated for the latter ceremony.

00:01:49.980 --> 00:01:54.540
Not long after, "The Banshees of Inisherin"&nbsp;
stars Colin Farrell and Brendan Gleeson&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:54.540 --> 00:01:58.980
were also said to have contracted COVID-19,&nbsp;
according to The Hollywood Reporter. The event&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:58.980 --> 00:02:03.240
saw "Inisherin" as the night's big winner,&nbsp;
with Farrell nabbing a win for best motion&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:03.240 --> 00:02:07.320
picture actor in a musical or comedy, Martin&nbsp;
McDonagh getting a win for best screenplay,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:07.320 --> 00:02:11.520
and the film itself winning best musical or&nbsp;
comedy motion picture. Per The Hollywood Reporter,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:11.520 --> 00:02:15.240
the COVID-19 diagnosis also means that&nbsp;
neither actor will be appearing at the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:15.240 --> 00:02:20.160
Critics Choice Awards. So what will happen&nbsp;
at upcoming award shows? Likely not much.

00:02:20.160 --> 00:02:24.660
The news of actors such as these contracting&nbsp;
COVID-19 following their appearance at the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:24.660 --> 00:02:28.260
Golden Globes highlights the reality&nbsp;
that we are still not fully out of the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:28.260 --> 00:02:32.880
COVID-19 pandemic. While vaccines and other&nbsp;
medical breakthroughs have helped the world&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:32.880 --> 00:02:36.840
readjust over the last few years, there are&nbsp;
still times of the year when the danger is&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:36.840 --> 00:02:40.560
more present. Such was the case for the&nbsp;
Golden Globes. Not long before the event,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:40.560 --> 00:02:45.300
LA Public Health issued a recommended 10-day&nbsp;
mask policy as people transition back into work&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:45.300 --> 00:02:50.340
and school. The Golden Globe ceremony this year,&nbsp;
however, largely seemed to abandon this mindset,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:50.340 --> 00:02:54.120
with the only major attendee seen&nbsp;
wearing a mask being Jessica Chastain.

00:02:54.120 --> 00:02:58.920
To some, this might cause concerns for the&nbsp;
upcoming 95th Academy Award ceremony. Although&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:58.920 --> 00:03:02.880
it's more than likely that Curtis, Farrell,&nbsp;
Gleeson, and any other Golden Globe attendees&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:02.880 --> 00:03:08.220
who contracted COVID-19 will recover by the time&nbsp;
the Oscars ceremony occurs on March 12th, 2023,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:08.220 --> 00:03:11.700
should the Academy be too relaxed&nbsp;
with their pandemic protocols,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:11.700 --> 00:03:15.420
we could see another string of sick&nbsp;
celebrities follow up the event. Thankfully,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:15.420 --> 00:03:18.840
the Academy's safety measures from last&nbsp;
year's event seemed to have worked out,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:18.840 --> 00:03:23.760
as no major news came out regarding confirmed&nbsp;
cases. Only time will tell how the results of this&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:23.760 --> 00:03:27.480
year's Globes will affect safety precautions&nbsp;
at other award shows in the coming months.

